%1$s</ul>' => '<h3><a name="doujutsu"></a>Doujutsu (Eye Techniques)</h3>
Some masters teach how to awaken a <b>doujutsu</b>, an eye technique. Eyes are awakened in long trainings (see above): Falcon Eye (Sand Village, level 12), Sharingan (Leaf Village, level 20), Byakugan (Mist Village, level 30, Chuunin), Celestial Eye (Heaven and Earth Hamlet, level 45, Jounin) and Rinnegan (Akatsuki Hideout, level 60, Jounin). Each eye has its own style: Falcon = accuracy, critical hits and ignores a bit of defense; Sharingan = agility, intelligence and dodge, plus attack and a chance to reflect the enemy’s blow at stage 4 (evolves in 4 stages); Byakugan = accuracy, ignores defense, more drops and sees what the enemy carries; Celestial = defense, luck, drops and the whole world map with no fog; Rinnegan = intelligence and a little attack and defense, with teleport and guaranteed escape, but burns Chakra very fast. The Chakra cost of every eye grows with level. The Rinnegan is not an evolution of the Sharingan.
<ul>
<li /><b>One eye at a time</b>: awakening another eye replaces the current one. The awakening training leaves the Training Panel when completed and can be redone to go back to an old eye.
<li /><b>Activate</b>: click the eye below your avatar (faded = off). While active it spends Chakra every few seconds, even if you don’t reload the page, and closes by itself when Chakra runs out. Doujutsu and Senjutsu can’t be active at the same time.
<li /><b>Bonuses</b>: they only count while the eye is open, in battles, duels and PvP (the opponent’s eye counts too). Nothing is added permanently to your attributes.
<li /><b>Sharingan evolution</b> (stages 1 to 4), through any of the paths: strong enemies defeated (level at least yours minus %2$s) with the Sharingan active (%3$s for stages 2, 3 and 4); duel wins since the current stage (%4$s); or the <b>Sharingan Evolution</b> training in the Leaf Village, redone for each stage.
<li /><b>Rinnegan Teleport</b> (Doujutsu screen): takes you to any coordinate of the map, with the Rinnegan active and outside battles and duels. It costs %5$s TP + %6$s per 10 squares, %7$s Chakra + %8$s per 10 squares and %9$s%% of max HP + %10$s%% per 10 squares (you must keep 1 HP). It doesn’t open portals inside villages.
</ul>
